NATURAL EARTH
Natural Earth map data is in the public domain. CartoRig credits:
"Made with Natural Earth. Free vector and raster map data @ naturalearthdata.com."

Pinned build source repository:
https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector
Exact source commit used by the Milestone A data build:
f1890d9f152c896d250a77557a5751a93d494776

Bundled runtime datasets generated from that checkout:
- Natural Earth 1:50m Land — source version 4.1.0.
  Source theme: 50m_physical/ne_50m_land.
  Installed runtime: data/ne_50m_land.lua.
- Natural Earth Admin 0 Countries — 1:50m, source version 5.1.1.
  Source theme: 50m_cultural/ne_50m_admin_0_countries.
  Installed runtime: per-feature Lua geometry under data/regions plus ne_catalog.tsv.
- Natural Earth Admin 1 States/Provinces — 1:10m, source version 5.1.1.
  Source theme: 10m_cultural/ne_10m_admin_1_states_provinces.
  Natural Earth's 1:50m Admin 1 v5.1.1 layer currently represents USA/Canada
  only, so CartoRig uses the 1:10m Natural Earth Admin 1 source for required
  subdivisions such as Mato Grosso. The actual 1:10m scale is persisted on each
  State object and is never presented as 1:50m.
- Natural Earth Populated Places — 1:50m, source version 5.1.2.
  Source theme: 50m_cultural/ne_50m_populated_places.
  Installed runtime: point records in ne_catalog.tsv.

The generated natural-earth-manifest.json records source commit, dataset version,
scale, coverage, source-file SHA-256 hashes, generated geometry counts and
generated runtime hashes. Geometry is generated in the CartoRig installer build; the end user
does not download or prepare geodata manually.

Natural Earth terms:
https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/

NSIS INSTALLER
- Build-time tool: NSIS 3.x from Chocolatey community packages on a standard
  free Windows the CartoRig installer build runner.
- The installed executable carries the NSIS zlib/libpng-licensed installer
  and uninstaller runtime. See https://nsis.sourceforge.io/Docs/AppendixI.html
- Runtime Fusion Fuses and scripts are Lua source; no proprietary Resolve SDK
  or DaVinci Resolve binaries are redistributed.

PYSH (PYSHAPEFILE)
- Build-time only dependency: pyshp 2.3.1.
- Used by the CartoRig installer build to read the pinned Natural Earth shapefiles and generate
  CartoRig's offline runtime representation.
- It is not installed on the end user's machine by CartoRig.
- Project: https://github.com/GeospatialPython/pyshp
- License: MIT.

No DaVinci Resolve binaries, proprietary SDK binaries, online map tiles or paid
services are bundled.
